{"birds": [{"name": "Blue Jay", "sci": "Cyanocitta cristata", "n": 4, "first": "9:21 AM", "last": "9:26 AM", "ts": 1795357287, "mins": [561, 561, 563, 566], "anim": null, "trunk": false, "fact": "That blue isn’t a pigment. Tiny structures in the feathers scatter light, which is why a crushed blue feather looks brown. Jays also bury acorns and help spread oak trees.", "vox": "sounds/voice/cyanocitta-cristata.mp3?v=1793112993", "snd": "sounds/cyanocitta-cristata.mp3?v=1793113328", "sndby": "Christopher McPherson, xeno-canto XC691163, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0", "key": "bluejay", "cm": 28.0, "img": "cutouts/bluejay.png?v=1793031427", "w": 385, "h": 369, "len": 474.0, "v": 1793031427, "beak": [0.99, 0.17, "R"], "mask": {"c": 32, "r": 31, "b": "AAAPgAAAD+AAAA/4AAAH+AAAD/8AAB//AAA//gAAf/AAAP/wAAH/8AAD//AAB//wAB//4AAf/+AAf//gAH//zAD//5wA//94Af+OcAP/8eAD9/fgA/l/gAPgHwAHgD4AHwA4AB8AeAA+AGAAfADgAHgAwADwAAAA4AAAAA=="}}, {"name": "Fish Crow", "sci": "Corvus ossifragus", "n": 3, "first": "9:21 AM", "last": "9:32 AM", "ts": 1795357295, "mins": [561, 571, 572], "anim": null, "trunk": false, "fact": "It looks just like an American Crow. The giveaway is the voice: a nasal, two-note “uh-uh” instead of a clear “caw.”", "vox": "sounds/voice/corvus-ossifragus.mp3?v=1793112991", "snd": "sounds/corvus-ossifragus.mp3?v=1793113105", "sndby": "Mike Nelson, xeno-canto XC130581, CC BY-NC-SA 3.0", "key": "fishcrow", "cm": 38.0, "img": "cutouts/fishcrow.png?v=1793990894", "w": 484, "h": 472, "len": 557.0, "v": 1793990894, "beak": [0.021, 0.08, "L"], "mask": {"c": 32, "r": 31, "b": "D4AAAH/AAAD/4AAAf/AAAA/4AAAH/AAAB/4AAAf/gAAH/8AAB//gAAf/+AAH//wAA//+AAH//wAB//+AAP//gAA//8AAH//gAA//+AAHZ/wAB2P8AA5h+AAcwP4f/uA+P//+Dj////4////+P////gD///4AAD/+AAAAPg=="}}, {"name": "House Finch", "sci": "Haemorhous mexicanus", "n": 15, "first": "9:24 AM", "last": "9:31 AM", "ts": 1795357462, "mins": [564, 565, 566, 566, 566, 567, 567, 568, 568, 569, 569, 570, 570, 571, 571], "anim": null, "trunk": false, "fact": "Native to the West, house finches were released on Long Island in 1940 as pet-shop “Hollywood finches” and spread across the East. Redder males are favored by females.", "vox": "sounds/voice/haemorhous-mexicanus.mp3?v=1793113005", "snd": "sounds/haemorhous-mexicanus.mp3?v=1793113108", "sndby": "Ted Floyd, xeno-canto XC622745, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0", "key": "housefinch", "cm": 14.0, "img": "cutouts/housefinch.png?v=1793046043", "w": 800, "h": 581, "len": 662.0, "v": 1793046043, "beak": [0.12, 0.13, "L"], "mask": {"c": 32, "r": 23, "b": "B+AAAAfwAQoP8AHOH/gB7wf8Af8D/gH/B/8A3wf/AP4H/4zgB//fwAP/zwAD//4AAf/+AAD//AAAf/gAAD/8AA/+/AAH4B4AB+APAB6AD4A4AAeA8AAAAMAAAAA="}}, {"name": "American Goldfinch", "sci": "Spinus tristis", "n": 2, "first": "9:30 AM", "last": "9:34 AM", "ts": 1795357821, "mins": [570, 574], "anim": null, "trunk": false, "fact": "One of the strictest vegetarians among birds. Goldfinches nest late in summer, when thistle seeds are ripe, and swap bright yellow for olive-brown in winter.", "vox": "sounds/voice/spinus-tristis.mp3?v=1793113053", "snd": "sounds/spinus-tristis.mp3?v=1793113090", "sndby": "Will Sweet, xeno-canto XC453934, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0", "key": "goldfinch", "cm": 12.0, "img": "cutouts/goldfinch.png?v=1793990895", "w": 451, "h": 369, "len": 415.0, "v": 1793990895, "beak": [0.206, 0.15, "L"], "mask": {"c": 32, "r": 26, "b": "ADwAAAD+AAAB/wAAA/8AAAP/gAAA/8AAAH/AAAD/8AAA//AAAP/4DwD/+B4Af/w4AH/+8AA//8AAP/8AAB//AAAH/4AAB//AAA/PwAAeQeAA/gHwAfgA+APIAHwPAAAgHAAAADgAAAA="}}, {"name": "Eastern Bluebird", "sci": "Sialia sialis", "n": 1, "first": "9:37 AM", "last": "9:37 AM", "ts": 1795358231, "mins": [577], "anim": null, "trunk": false, "fact": "Bluebirds nest in tree cavities, and their numbers crashed in the early 1900s when starlings and house sparrows took the holes. Volunteer nest-box trails helped them rebound.", "vox": "sounds/voice/sialia-sialis.mp3?v=1793113046", "snd": "sounds/sialia-sialis.mp3?v=1793113130", "sndby": "Robin Carter, xeno-canto XC1374, CC BY-NC-ND 2.5", "key": "bluebird", "cm": 18.0, "img": "cutouts/bluebird.png?v=1793990893", "w": 649, "h": 609, "len": 744.0, "v": 1793990893, "beak": [0.851, 0.1, "R"], "mask": {"c": 32, "r": 30, "b": "AAA/AAAA/4AAAP/wAAH/4AAD/4AAA/+AAAP/gAAH/4AAD/+AAA//gAAf/4AAP/+AAD//gAB//4AA//8AAf/+AgH//g4D//w8A//48Af/98AP//8AH8b8AB8P8AAcPzAAOfgwAHPgAADvgAAA3gAAAHgAAABwAAAA"}}], "also": [], "date": "Sunday, November 22", "where": "", "updated": "9:37 AM", "sun": null, "wx": {"t": 58, "kind": "cloudy", "word": "Cloudy", "hi": 68, "lo": 52}, "code": "10a791c1d1", "listen": {"state": "on", "since": null, "control": false}}